T24-FR-1 - The HSM client writes the decrypted secret, the request and the raw response to the log (Blocker)
Category: MustChange/rewrite Priority: Blocker
Evidence: HSM_comun.cs:68 (../../General/T24/Aplicacion/Servicios/Comunes/HSM_comun.cs#L68) (request), HSM_comun.cs:72 (../../General/T24/Aplicacion/Servicios/Comunes/HSM_comun.cs#L72) (raw HSM response), HSM_comun.cs:76 (../../General/T24/Aplicacion/Servicios/Comunes/HSM_comun.cs#L76) (the interpreted, decrypted response), HSM_comun.cs:194 (../../General/T24/Aplicacion/Servicios/Comunes/HSM_comun.cs#L194) (the framed request), the callers that decrypt the BBVA PKCS#12 password and the BBVA digital key (SER_PAY.cs:648-662 (../../General/T24/Aplicacion/Servicios/Operaciones/SER_PAY.cs#L648-L662), TAX_PAY.cs:783-791 (../../General/T24/Aplicacion/Servicios/Operaciones/TAX_PAY.cs#L783-L791)) and the list of parameters the project itself declares sensitive (ConstantesServicio.cs:17 (../../General/T24/Aplicacion/Enums/ConstantesServicio.cs#L17)).
Code block (csharp)
// HSM_comun.cs:72-76 - every decryption logs the answer, then the interpreted (clear) answer
Config.EscribirLog("INFO|HSM.DecryptPasswordStore|Respuesta: " + lsResponse);
lsResponse = InterpretHSMResponse(lsResponse, lsCommand);
Config.EscribirLog("INFO|HSM.DecryptPasswordStore|Respuesta final: " + lsResponse);
Issue / impact: DecryptParametersStore is the path through which SER_PAY and TAX_PAY obtain the BBVA PKCS#12 password and the BBVA digital key. After InterpretHSMResponse the string is the clear value (hex encoded, which Hex2Ascii turns into text in the caller), so one INFO line per payment attempt puts the secret into the service log; the request line adds the key label, the KCV and the encrypted node. The project masks such values elsewhere (the key list in ConstantesServicio and the logger masks key=value shapes), but these lines have no key=value form and are not masked. Anyone with read access to the log folder or its backups can recover the credentials that the HSM exists to protect.
Recommended change: Delete the four log lines (or log only the command name, the length of the answer and whether the KCV check passed). Treat every credential decrypted since this code shipped as exposed: rotate the BBVA PKCS#12 password and the digital key, purge or restrict the log history, and add a unit test that fails when a log argument contains the decrypted value.
Benefit: The HSM keeps its purpose: the clear secret exists only in memory for the duration of the call.
Suggested JIRA: T24-FR-1 (Blocker, MustChange/rewrite).
T24-FR-2 - The T24 authorizer user name and password are written to the log inside the OFS string (Blocker)
Category: MustChange/rewrite Priority: Blocker
